#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# legendre_p

#% text
# `legendre_p(n, x)` gives the Legendre polynomial P_n(x).

#% text
# `legendre_p(n, m, x)` gives the associated Legendre function P_n^m(x).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# At a non-negative integer degree the polynomial is expanded in its argument (evaluated for numbers).

#% item
# At other numeric degrees the hypergeometric representation gives the value; symbolic degrees stay unevaluated.

#% item
# The associated functions include the factor (-1)^m (1 - x^2)^(m/2).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
legendre_p(3, x)
#% output
#= (-3/2)*x + (5/2)*x^3

#% cell
legendre_p(2, 1, x)
#% output
#= -3*x*(1 - x^2)^(1/2)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
legendre_p(1/2, 0.3)
#% output
#= 0.7009385309696551

#% cell
legendre_p(3, 0.25)
#% output
#= -0.3359375

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `legendre_q`, `spherical_harmonic_y`
